  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between S-sulphocysteine and L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain, mediated through multiple intermediate targets. S-sulphocysteine is identified as a target of several compounds, including 3-Acetyl-11-(3-Methylbutanoyl)-13-Propanoylilikonapyrone, cis-Isopinocamphone, and Mollicelline K, all of which are implicated in targeting L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. This indicates that S-sulphocysteine may act as a modulator or inhibitor of this enzyme, possibly through a common mechanism involving the interaction with these compounds. The presence of multiple distinct targets for S-sulphocysteine, each leading to the same final target, suggests a possible role in regulating the activity of L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for S-sulphocysteine to influence the enzyme's function, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional role of S-sulphocysteine in this process.",
